<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica's Mercantile Lisbon bank lifts 1996 income.</title>
<headline>SAfrica's Mercantile Lisbon bank lifts 1996 income.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    40.1	    vs 40.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    12.6	    vs  -</p>
<p>Income before retained</p>
<p>     earnings of associates  17.84	   vs 11.68</p>
<p>    Share of associates	 1.14	   vs  0.13 loss</p>
<p>    Income after tax	   18.89	   vs 11.56</p>
<p>    Net interest income     116.79	   vs 93.02</p>
<p>    Other operating income   98.85	   vs 83.85</p>
<p>    Bad/doubtful debt charge 14.29	   vs  9.66</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			23.76	   vs 17.77</p>
<p>    Tax			     5.92	   vs  6.02</p>
<p>Full name: Mercantile Lisbon Bank Holdings Ltd, unlisted</p>
<p>NOTE - Flat EPS reflects increased shares in issue.</p>
<p>The company said shareholders had committed to add a further 143 million rand to its capital base to fund expansion.</p>
<p>Total assets increased from 1.8 bilion rand to 2.4 billion while the depositors' book reached 2.2 billion rand. Mercantile Bank Ltd, the banking subsidiary of the holding company, registered a 28.3 percent growth in advances.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
